{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>אל</b> — The prophet relates what the wicked family would say to the prophets of HaShem: <b>לא תנבאו</b> (you shall not prophesy) — you shall not preach. Thus <b>ככה יטיפון</b> (so they would preach to them): they would preach to them, 'Do not preach.'" "The word <b>יסג</b>, with samekh and shin, comes in a pa'al (light) pattern in place of pi'el (heavy), to say ישג in place of ישיג. For whoever does not preach to this family — disgrace will not overtake him."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:42.554921932Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}